Implementing a multi-tree list (also known as a hierarchical tree view) within an Angular application involves several steps. Here's a basic guide to help you get started:

### Step 1: Set Up Your Project

If you haven't already set up your Angular project, do so using the following commands:

```bash
ng new my-app
cd my-app
```

Then install the necessary packages:

```bash
npm install @angular/material --save
npm install @angular/cdk --save
npm install @types/node --save-dev
```

Install Material and Cdk for UI components.

### Step 2: Create Tree Data Structure

First, let's create some sample data that we can use to demonstrate the multi-tree list functionality.

In `src/app/my-component.ts`:
```typescript
import { Component } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-my-component',
  templateUrl: './my-component.component.html'
})
export class MyComponent {
  public items = [
    {
      id: 0,
      name: 'Root Node 1',
      children: [
        {
          id: 1,
          name: 'Child Node 1-1',
          children: [
            { id: 2, name: 'Grandchild Node 1-1-1' }
          ]
        },
        {
          id: 3,
          name: 'Child Node 1-2'
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      id: 4,
      name: 'Root Node 2',
      children: [
        {
          id: 5,
          name: 'Child Node 2-1',
          children: []
        }
      ]
    }
  ];
}
```

### Step 3: Create Multi-Tree List Template

Now, let's create the template part of our component.

In `src/app/my-component.component.html`:
```html
<div *ngFor="let item of items">
  <h2>{{ item.name }}</h2>

  <!-- Display child nodes recursively -->
  <div *ngIf="item.children && item.children.length > 0" class="tree-list">
    <ul>
      <li *ngFor="let child of item.children">{{ child.name }}<br></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

</div>
```

### Step 4: Implement Drag-and-Drop Behavior

To enable drag-and-drop behavior on the tree structure, you'll need to use Angular Material's `MatTreeNode` or its equivalent from Cdk. Since this is a simple example, I'll assume you're using MatTreeNode.

